---
import ToolLayout from '../../layouts/ToolLayout.astro';
import JsonDiff from '../../components/JsonDiff.jsx';
---
<ToolLayout title="JSON Diff Checker" description="Compare two JSON objects and see exactly what was added, removed, or changed.">
  <JsonDiff client:load slot="tool" />
  <h2>When this helps</h2>
  <p>Useful for comparing API responses before/after a change, config file versions, or debugging why two "identical-looking" payloads behave differently.</p>

  <h2>Common JSON Diff Mistakes</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Assuming key order matters</strong> in JSON objects — semantically identical JSON with reordered keys shouldn't be treated as "different" for most purposes.</li>
    <li><strong>Not noticing type differences</strong> (like a number vs. a string representation of the same value), which a simple text diff might miss but a JSON-aware diff catches.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>When to Use This JSON Diff Checker</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Comparing an API response before and after a backend change</li>
    <li>Debugging why two config files that "look the same" behave differently</li>
    <li>Reviewing what changed in a JSON payload during testing</li>
  </ul>
</ToolLayout>
